WEBVTT

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:09.720
The loss to the Vulcan people is incalculable.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.870
Pajem was one of our most revered sanctuaries.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:18.230
Ambassador, we are very sorry for your loss.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.600
But with all due respect, the High Command has to take some responsibility.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:25.680
You were using the monastery as a surveillance station.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:28.580
We were observing a dangerous and aggressive neighbor.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:34.090
The Andorians wouldn't have found the station if your people hadn't interfered.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:40.130
They've been in space for six months, and they've already destabilized an entire sector.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.530
I'm afraid I can't agree with that, Ambassador.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:45.810
This was a volatile situation long before Starfleet got involved.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.130
Perhaps if you'd been a little more open with us, this tragedy might have been avoided.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.660
We warned you something like this would happen.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:56.970
He's too impulsive.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:00:59.980
Captain Gardner would have made a far more...

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.710
suitable commanding officer the Vulcan consulate doesn't make command

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:18.480
assignments here there was a time when your people sought our guidance I regret

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:24.230
that time has passed I've been recalled the Vulcan for consultation in the

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:27.980
meantime our joint fleet operations have been suspended

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:38.680
Yes, Ephraim?

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.200
Get me Captain Archer.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:40.930
Bye, sir.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:05.590
And I will see my dream come alive and last.

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:08.640
I will touch the sky.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.540
They're not gonna hold me down no more.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:16.510
No, they're not gonna change my mind.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:20.560
Cause I've got faith of the heart.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:16.610
We're having some changed course overnight.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:19.110
Found a new system in the Vulcan database.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.230
Corridan. They're only a few light years away,

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:23.830
so I thought we'd, uh, take a look.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:28.630
Inhabited? Just over three billion humanoids.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:29.960
Apparently, the Vulcan...

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:37.020
I had Hoshi send a message to their Chancellor and she invited us to visit their capital city.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:38.940
I'll start shining my boots.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:43.930
I think I'll just take Hoshi.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:45.300
This time?

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:51.620
The Chancellor asked me to limit the number of people I bring down until they get to know us better.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:53.260
Oh.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:55.840
That's really too bad.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.960
According to the database, they've got the largest...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.360
starship construction yards in the sector they're supposed to have ships that can

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:10.770
run circles around the Vulcans better than 65 they say some cordon ships have

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:20.800
reached warp seven but that's just a rumor warp seven you should lend Hoshi

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:24.080
your camera I'll be sure she takes lots of pictures

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.770
Ah, you had me going there for a minute.

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:38.270
You're just too easy a target.

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:39.730
So you're taking me, right?

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:40.830
Bridge to Captain Archer.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:45.290
Go ahead.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.170
Receiving a transmission from Starfleet Command.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:49.680
It's Admiral Forrest, sir.

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:54.070
Was anyone killed?

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:56.950
The Andorians gave the monks three hours

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:58.450
before they started their bombardment.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:04:59.970
Fortunately, they all got

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:02.740
How are the Vulcans taking this?

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:04.670
Not well.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:10.710
I can't really blame the Andorians for reacting this way.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:13.160
If the roles were reversed,

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.980
the Vulcans might have done the same thing.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:17.780
Vulcans may have good reason for keeping an eye on them.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:18.620
I've seen the reports.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:22.600
These Andorian commandos are a dangerous group.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:25.220
That's the same crap the Vulcans used to say about us.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:27.370
John, you're doing a lot of good work,

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:29.660
but you've got to be more careful.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:33.630
can't be getting involved in interspecies conflicts.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:37.490
I understand.

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:41.840
I'm afraid I've got some more bad news.

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:17.710
Come in, Forrest.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:24.540
No easy way to say this.

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:29.650
Indorians destroyed the sanctuary at Bajam.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:36.120
Were there any survivors?

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:44.880
Unfortunately, the monks and the intelligence operatives were given advance warning.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:45.620
They're fine.

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:48.410
Was there time to remove any of the relics?

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:49.410
I don't know.

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:53.810
Command believes we're to blame for this.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:59.980
They're sending a sh...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.940
to take you back to Vulcan.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:04.600
We'll be here in two days.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:12.700
I won't have time to complete my scans of this sector.

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.560
I'll ask Ensign Mayweather to finish them.

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:18.030
Maybe I wasn't clear.

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:23.410
This isn't a temporary transfer.

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:25.430
They're reassigning you.

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:27.970
I understand the situation, Captain.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:29.980
I'm certain...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.270
command will find you a suitable replacement am i the only one who has a problem with this

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:42.340
because you seem perfectly fine my assignment to the enterprise was only supposed to last

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:50.010
eight days it was unrealistic to expect it to continue indefinitely high command is looking

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:56.440
for a scapegoat someone to blame they can't punish me so they're taking it out on my science

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:59.720
Sounds like an emotional reaction.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:08.250
if you ask me i am largely responsible for what happened don't give yourself too much credit

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:14.670
i was the one who found pajama in the database and i led the landing party i want you to know

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:19.590
i'm filing a protest with a high command that won't make any difference you don't know that

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:26.360
captain i was assigned to enterprise not simply as an observer but to represent the interests of

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:29.870
the vulcan people it's clear in the eyes

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:39.820
my superiors I haven't done that they have no right to do this to you crew for

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:49.100
another 48 hours is there anything else

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:02.910
This is just another part of the joke, right?

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:05.230
I'm sorry, Tripp. I've got to take to Paul on this one.

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:08.630
I need to spend some time with her alone.

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:10.740
No, I know you're pulling my leg.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:13.820
Paul's being transferred.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:16.690
The ship's on its way to take her back.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.400
What? Meet me for lunch. I'll fill you in.

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:26.020
Really?

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:31.600
I just heard about your transfer.

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:34.010
I'm sorry you'll be leaving us.

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:39.580
I'm sure you'll excel at whatever new assignment you're given.

00:09:40.950 --> 00:09:42.570
I haven't received another assignment.

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:45.790
I assumed you were being promoted.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:50.660
My superiors believe that I'm responsible for the destruction of the Pajam Sanctuary.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:53.460
Do you agree with their assessment?

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:57.390
It's the logical conclusion.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:09:59.970
I'm certainly high comm...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.580
Would reconsider your transfer if they knew everything you've done for this crew?

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:08.740
You realize you're not the first Vulcan officer to be posted aboard a human starship.

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:15.650
High Command has tried this before, but none of the others lasted more than a few weeks.

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:19.360
They found their crewmates too chaotic and unpredictable.

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:26.680
But you've been here more than six months, and you haven't merely tolerated this crew to become part of it.

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:29.980
Isn't it logical to take...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:41.140
pride in that accomplishment pride is a human indulgence i suppose it is oh i have it under

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:45.940
authority but several crew members are planning a gathering in your honor i believe it's called a

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:50.270
going away party i'd keep on alert if i were you

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:13.160
So, what do you know about Corridor?

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:16.060
There are three billion inhabitants,

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:19.710
mostly concentrated in several cities in the equatorial region.

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:22.280
I wasn't asking for the statistics.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.320
Your people have been coming here for decades.

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:27.060
You must know something about their culture.

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:29.680
The kinds of food they eat.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:31.340
They do for fun.

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:33.660
The Vulcan database doesn't contain that information.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:36.020
Of course not.

00:11:38.410 --> 00:11:40.370
I'm uncertain why I was chosen for this mission.

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:44.340
These people have never seen humans before.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:48.720
It makes sense for someone with a familiar face to make the introductions.

00:11:51.340 --> 00:11:53.980
I have a lot of work to complete before the Vulcan ship arrives.

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:55.260
Don't worry.

00:11:56.390 --> 00:11:57.970
I'll get you back in plenty of time.

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:08.330
I just thought you might enjoy one final mission with your captain.

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:14.780
Or maybe I should just take you back to Enterprise.

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:19.740
We're only a few minutes from the capital.

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:22.490
Returning to this ship now would be a waste of fuel.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:36.380
Tries to cap Nartzer.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:39.020
Go ahead, Trep.

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:41.280
We're raiding the ship, closing on you fast.

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:44.350
I got it.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:46.520
Some kind of fixed-wing aircraft.

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:49.330
Did the Chancellor say anything about sending an escort?

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:53.320
I don't think they're an escort.

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:58.400
Alien vessel, reduced to one-quarter power and adjust heading to 317 Mark V.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:12:59.960
I'm taking evasive action.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.910
Bring the plasma weapons online.

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:04.300
Ready.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:05.180
Fire.

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:32.880
Houdini could get out of this.

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:36.260
Perhaps you should invite him on your next mission.

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:41.080
Harry Houdini was a magician, an escape artist.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:46.650
He was famous for being able to free himself from any kind of restraint.

00:13:47.050 --> 00:13:49.430
Rope, chains, anything.

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:52.580
That seems unlikely.

00:13:54.470 --> 00:13:55.950
That's why he was called a magician.

00:13:58.080 --> 00:13:59.680
Some people say he was double-jointed.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:05.690
I don't suppose Vulcans are double-jointed?

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:07.680
Unfortunately not.

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:23.540
Uh, Vulcan, what brings you to Corrigan?

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:25.760
You want answers, talk to me.

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:27.950
You're her superior?

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:29.500
That's right.

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:31.640
I don't recognize your species.

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:35.230
I'm human from the planet Earth.

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:38.620
Never heard of Vulcans taking orders from anyone.

00:14:41.220 --> 00:14:42.400
There's been a misunderstanding.

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:45.250
We're here at the invitation of your Chancellor.

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:47.050
He's not my Chancellor.

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:50.640
That government is kept in power by the Vulcans.

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:53.280
If you're with them, you're on the wrong side.

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:57.770
What kind of weapon is this?

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:02.280
You won't tell me.

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:03.540
It's a phase pistol.

00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:06.950
We'll put these to good use.

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:11.330
I'm curious about your starship.

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:12.410
What can you tell me about it?

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:16.260
Our protein resequencer can make chicken sandwiches.

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:18.320
Stop!

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:21.260
He's not a tactical officer.

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:24.290
He's the ship's steward.

00:15:29.460 --> 00:15:29.900
We're here.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:33.150
I'm here to prepare a banquet for your chancellor.

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:39.810
Your people have a reputation for truthfulness.

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:42.230
You wouldn't be lying to me, would you, Vulcan?

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:48.750
Now I understand. You're the captain, aren't you?

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:51.980
Perhaps.

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:57.720
Whoever you are, you picked the wrong time for a visit.

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:12.320
A steward.

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:24.250
Your shuttle was forced down by members of a radical faction.

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:29.930
Since the attack took place outside our sensor grid, your officers won't...

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:36.870
be easy to find. You didn't tell us about any factions. They're a small group. We had no idea

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:42.470
they were capable of an attack like this. But be assured, Commander, your people are almost certainly

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:48.920
still alive. Almost certainly. The radicals will want something in exchange for the hostages. They

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:56.270
always do. Sidearms, dicobalt explosives. It's important that you don't give them anything. Is

00:16:56.270 --> 00:16:59.980
this how you protect your visitors? You might have told us about your little war before.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:06.220
you invited us down we're not at war commander this is an isolated incident i don't care what

00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:12.180
you call it we just want to know where our people are we are doing everything in our power to find

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:19.440
them i'm gonna sit on our hands and wait for a ransom note start scanning for human and vulcan

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:23.620
bioscience there are billions of people down there it could take days it might be easier to

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:28.800
locate the shuttle pod i'll try but if the pod's been powered down it's almost impossible to pick up

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:29.240
It's signature.

00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:32.320
We've got to start somewhere.

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:36.000
Ready?

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:37.650
Yes.

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:38.670
Go.

00:17:40.150 --> 00:17:40.610
Easy.

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:07.990
I think we got a little higher that time.

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:10.930
Only a few centimeters.

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:14.060
That's not frustration I hear in your voice.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:17.270
No.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:18.340
Good.

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:20.500
Try it again.

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:22.600
One, two.

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:27.390
Yeah.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.180
Ready?

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:31.320
Yes.

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:48.750
I think these are starting to come loose.

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:50.470
How about yours?

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:52.730
Slightly.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:57.770
We can turn around, chase each other.

00:18:58.270 --> 00:18:59.490
We might be able to untie these knots.

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:11.390
I think the Vulcan database might have mentioned

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:13.730
these people were fighting a civil war.

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:15.270
The database is accurate.

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:20.270
The Coridan government doesn't view this as a civil war.

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:24.280
I imagine your people are going to want their database back, too.

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:25.720
Well, they can have it.

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:35.550
Can you reach the knot?

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:39.210
I believe so.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.610
Without the database, you wouldn't have found this planet.

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:49.160
Or Pijam.

00:19:49.650 --> 00:19:51.450
You're not responsible for what happened.

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:59.440
I didn't have any idea that your people had installed a listening post.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:06.340
Oh, that they were Andorian commandos there.

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:12.300
Enterprise had no good reason to visit a Vulcan sanctuary.

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:17.440
I had the opportunity to protest, but I chose not to.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:28.050
It's clear that living among humans has caused my reasoning to become compromised.

00:20:30.280 --> 00:20:34.090
I think I understand you're running away

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:37.210
because you're afraid to become one of us.

00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:40.180
I am not running away.

00:20:40.360 --> 00:20:41.760
Then why aren't you fighting this transfer?

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:56.080
People took something away from my father

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:57.040
that meant a lot to him.

00:20:57.510 --> 00:20:59.150
They're not gonna do the same thing to me.

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:04.450
Thank you.

00:22:03.580 --> 00:22:07.650
It's definitely a titanium signature, about four kilometers outside the capital.

00:22:08.690 --> 00:22:09.890
Practically under their noses.

00:22:10.180 --> 00:22:13.710
From what we can tell, the entire capital is surrounded by a shantytown.

00:22:13.980 --> 00:22:17.990
There are almost as many biosigns on the outskirts as there are inside the city.

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:21.490
Looks like these people have a lot to learn about building a free society.

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:24.210
Have you found human or Vulcan biosigns?

00:22:24.690 --> 00:22:26.880
Not yet. The part's transpired.

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:28.390
They must have switched it off, sir.

00:22:28.900 --> 00:22:29.980
I've got a rescue team stand-

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:35.700
behind the lunch bay hold on Malcolm we don't even know if this is our pod I don't want to go

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:42.910
down and find it some alien tractor it's our shuttle pod I'm certain of it all I'm suggesting

00:22:42.910 --> 00:22:50.000
is we go down and have a look around sir we're being hailed audio only who is it can't tell

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:59.940
put them through it's enterprise yes and you are we're holding your cat

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:04.020
and your steward in exchange for their safe return we want 40 of your phase

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:09.390
weapons the same type we found aboard your shuttle he hailed at this time

00:23:09.390 --> 00:23:14.600
tomorrow wait let me talk to the cap I'm sure you wouldn't want any harm to come

00:23:14.600 --> 00:23:20.780
to her we'll rely on your full compliance hello they've cut transmission

00:23:20.780 --> 00:23:26.120
we're able to trace it they're using the tracks lighting signal they call the

00:23:26.120 --> 00:23:29.680
captain her are we sure they've got the right hostages

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:31.750
At least it sounds like they're still alive.

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:32.940
For how long?

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:34.960
We don't have 40 face pistols.

00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:35.720
We've got 15.

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:39.190
And even if we give them to these people, there's no guarantee they'll keep their word.

00:23:39.900 --> 00:23:41.220
We know where the shuttle is.

00:23:41.800 --> 00:23:44.620
We have to send a team down now while we still have the element of surprise.

00:23:47.370 --> 00:23:48.570
We're getting another transmission.

00:23:49.570 --> 00:23:50.830
Probably thought of something else they want.

00:23:51.300 --> 00:23:52.300
It's not from the planet.

00:23:52.580 --> 00:23:54.760
It's coming from a Vulcan ship, the Navarre.

00:23:57.560 --> 00:23:58.040
Put it up.

00:24:01.980 --> 00:24:02.780
Where's Captain Archer?

00:24:03.964 --> 00:24:04.984
He's not here right now.

00:24:05.724 --> 00:24:06.344
Can I help you?

00:24:06.908 --> 00:24:09.108
Inform him that we'll be arriving within the hour.

00:24:10.524 --> 00:24:13.444
You guys made great time. We weren't expecting you until tomorrow.

00:24:14.204 --> 00:24:16.264
You obviously made an error in your calculations.

00:24:17.084 --> 00:24:20.324
Please have Sub-Commander T'Pol ready to depart when we arrive.

00:24:23.516 --> 00:24:24.556
We've got a...

00:24:25.628 --> 00:24:26.388
Bit of a problem.

00:24:27.644 --> 00:24:28.524
She's not here either.

00:24:29.372 --> 00:24:29.972
She in the cap.

00:24:30.030 --> 00:24:32.110
were on their way to the capital city when they were kidnapped.

00:24:34.190 --> 00:24:34.590
Convenient.

00:24:34.690 --> 00:24:36.810
I'm telling you, they were kidnapped.

00:24:37.170 --> 00:24:38.580
How do you know this?

00:24:38.840 --> 00:24:41.520
Maybe the ransom demand we just received gave us a clue.

00:24:41.720 --> 00:24:44.360
They threatened to kill them both if we didn't give them what they want.

00:24:45.480 --> 00:24:48.150
would be irrational to kill the hostages.

00:24:48.250 --> 00:24:50.230
They would lose their negotiating position.

00:24:51.240 --> 00:24:53.600
Maybe we're not dealing with the most rational people down there.

00:24:53.640 --> 00:24:54.320
Did you consider that?

00:24:54.420 --> 00:24:57.870
Since this situation involves a Vulcan officer,

00:24:58.010 --> 00:24:59.980
we will take over the...

00:25:00.060 --> 00:25:04.760
investigation. It would be best if you refrained from any foolish endeavors.

00:25:05.120 --> 00:25:11.880
What the hell is that supposed to... I'm getting real sick of being cut off.

00:25:23.830 --> 00:25:26.370
Your vessel is ill-equipped to mount a rescue mission.

00:25:26.570 --> 00:25:28.730
You would most likely become captive yourselves.

00:25:31.020 --> 00:25:32.780
My team will penetrate their base of operations.

00:25:33.100 --> 00:25:34.240
What does that mean?

00:25:34.920 --> 00:25:36.560
Sounds to me like you're planning an assault.

00:25:36.800 --> 00:25:39.790
Did it ever occur to you that that could get the captain and T'Pol killed?

00:25:40.240 --> 00:25:42.100
We've dealt with this sort of threat in the past.

00:25:42.120 --> 00:25:43.960
Swift, decisive action.

00:25:45.030 --> 00:25:45.970
is the logical response.

00:25:46.450 --> 00:25:49.390
You're awfully trigger happy for someone who's repressed his emotions.

00:25:49.790 --> 00:25:51.660
They've threatened the life of a Vulcan officer.

00:25:51.860 --> 00:25:55.620
We must discourage any such incidents in the future.

00:25:55.920 --> 00:25:56.960
This isn't your planet.

00:25:57.620 --> 00:25:59.860
Maybe the Corridan government has something to say about this.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:04.760
I've already been in contact with the Chancellor. She's given me full authority to implement this action.

00:26:05.330 --> 00:26:07.310
You don't really care what happens to them, do you?

00:26:08.040 --> 00:26:10.220
You probably wouldn't mind if they got caught in the crossfire.

00:26:10.670 --> 00:26:13.090
You'd consider it payback for what happened at Pijin.

00:26:13.890 --> 00:26:16.050
It's not Vulcan policy to negotiate with terrorists.

00:26:20.760 --> 00:26:22.020
Not even if it saves lives.

00:26:27.810 --> 00:26:29.910
Any data you may have on the location.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:32.850
of your captain and the subcommander would be useful.

00:26:36.820 --> 00:26:38.850
Sorry, we don't have anything.

00:27:16.988 --> 00:27:17.768
Can't eat like this.

00:27:48.908 --> 00:27:50.908
Can I pick up yours?

00:28:02.460 --> 00:28:03.420
Dig in, Sub-Commander.

00:28:04.760 --> 00:28:07.160
I don't think you'll be able to send this back for some plumic broth.

00:28:08.760 --> 00:28:09.600
I'm not hungry.

00:28:10.340 --> 00:28:11.360
I didn't ask if you were hungry.

00:28:12.020 --> 00:28:13.100
You need to keep up your strength.

00:28:15.450 --> 00:28:16.130
So eat.

00:28:16.970 --> 00:28:17.570
That's an order.

00:29:06.400 --> 00:29:10.270
We're being hailed, the Vulcans.

00:29:10.430 --> 00:29:12.480
Here you go.

00:29:14.140 --> 00:29:16.040
This is Sopek. Where's Commander Tucker?

00:29:16.860 --> 00:29:18.800
He's unavailable at the moment. Can I take a message?

00:29:19.100 --> 00:29:21.170
I want to know where that shuttle pod was going.

00:29:21.910 --> 00:29:22.870
What shuttle pod is that?

00:29:23.460 --> 00:29:26.060
The one that left your launch bay nine minutes ago.

00:29:28.740 --> 00:29:29.860
I really wouldn't know, sir.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:32.620
We get shuttle pods coming and going all the time.

00:29:32.620 --> 00:29:34.940
It's a little like Union Station around here.

00:29:35.520 --> 00:29:37.180
I want to know where Commander Tucker is.

00:29:37.520 --> 00:29:39.520
I'm sorry, your transmission's breaking up.

00:29:40.220 --> 00:29:53.820
I guess not everyone gets to live in Emerald City.

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:54.200
Yeah.

00:30:29.240 --> 00:30:29.960
listened to the volume.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:33.180
He warned you against doing anything foolish.

00:30:34.960 --> 00:30:36.780
What the hell are you doing here?

00:30:37.510 --> 00:30:38.790
Looking out for you pinkskins.

00:30:40.540 --> 00:30:45.360
If you had gone anywhere near that shuttle pod, you'd have been killed.

00:30:46.440 --> 00:30:49.020
They left it in the open for you to find.

00:30:51.560 --> 00:30:54.280
How do you know what Sopek told me? That was a secure transmission.

00:30:55.340 --> 00:30:57.620
Sopek is the senior Vulcan officer in the sector.

00:30:57.760 --> 00:30:59.860
Naturally, we keep him under close surveillance.

00:31:00.190 --> 00:31:07.680
We've been monitoring all Vulcan transmissions and ship deployments since the incident at Pajim.

00:31:08.970 --> 00:31:13.740
We know they're preparing for a war against us.

00:31:14.870 --> 00:31:17.610
I'm no fan of the Vulcans, but they're not warmongers.

00:31:17.860 --> 00:31:21.520
There's already a war going on, and the Vulcans are in the middle of it.

00:31:22.220 --> 00:31:27.120
Several rebel factions here are working to overthrow their government, a corrupt government,

00:31:27.140 --> 00:31:29.940
that has very close ties to your peace-loving.

00:31:30.120 --> 00:31:40.820
logical friends so you and the rebels figure you both have a common enemy the hostage takers have

00:31:40.820 --> 00:31:47.940
no plans to return your captain or the female would you deliver the weapons they'll be killed

00:31:49.280 --> 00:31:57.110
fortunately for you we have a relationship with the downtrodden here you tried to kill us last

00:31:57.110 --> 00:31:59.900
time we met why

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:08.140
trying to help us now I haven't slept well since our encounter at the Vulcan

00:32:08.140 --> 00:32:13.730
sanctuary I don't like being indebted to anyone least of all your captain you're

00:32:17.880 --> 00:32:24.290
right you never would have found that spy station without his help once he's free

00:32:24.290 --> 00:32:28.350
my debt will be repaid in full

00:32:30.800 --> 00:32:41.070
Shuttle, your people are being held here.

00:32:42.300 --> 00:32:43.760
These are barracks for the guards.

00:32:44.300 --> 00:32:44.680
How many?

00:32:45.010 --> 00:32:46.930
At least four inside the compound,

00:32:47.170 --> 00:32:49.090
two more up on the wall here,

00:32:49.370 --> 00:32:51.030
and two guards outside the gate,

00:32:51.090 --> 00:32:53.230
all armed with particle weapons.

00:32:53.870 --> 00:32:55.190
How'd you get this level of detail?

00:32:55.450 --> 00:32:57.390
We have an operative inside the compound.

00:33:00.480 --> 00:33:02.080
Unless he's going to take out these guards,

00:33:03.030 --> 00:33:05.570
you're not going to have an easy time getting all the way to the hostages.

00:33:05.910 --> 00:33:07.170
It's not your concern.

00:33:08.370 --> 00:33:09.870
It is if you get the captain killed.

00:33:11.630 --> 00:33:13.030
You're outnumbered four to one.

00:33:15.090 --> 00:33:16.370
Wouldn't you like to improve those odds?

00:33:18.820 --> 00:33:19.840
It could be useful.

00:33:24.360 --> 00:33:25.060
Give them their weapons.

00:33:35.920 --> 00:33:36.200
Tripp?

00:33:37.980 --> 00:33:38.260
Sir.

00:33:42.570 --> 00:33:42.930
Two of you?

00:33:43.890 --> 00:33:44.250
Exactly.

00:33:45.280 --> 00:33:46.560
With some old friends down here.

00:33:47.300 --> 00:33:49.610
It's apparently one of them thinks he owes you a favor.

00:33:50.110 --> 00:33:52.140
Wouldn't have picked a better time.

00:33:53.950 --> 00:33:56.380
Guard, you working with Natasha?

00:33:57.150 --> 00:33:59.160
Hey, 20 meters from...

00:34:00.410 --> 00:34:02.680
Until he shows up, just sit tight.

00:34:04.100 --> 00:34:05.240
That won't be a problem.

00:34:31.690 --> 00:34:36.350
Andorian ale warm you up

00:35:09.020 --> 00:35:09.380
Who's that?

00:35:10.170 --> 00:35:11.290
That's just my friend.

00:35:11.510 --> 00:35:12.090
Nothing to...

00:36:32.590 --> 00:36:33.570
We've got to get him out of there.

00:37:00.090 --> 00:37:00.870
Good to see you, Captain.

00:37:02.180 --> 00:37:03.220
Yeah, what's going on?

00:37:03.570 --> 00:37:05.070
The Vulcan's crashed our rescue party.

00:37:16.950 --> 00:37:21.840
The leaves is yours.

00:37:22.020 --> 00:37:26.040
It's the scammer she gave me from the Vulcan listening post.

00:37:26.630 --> 00:37:28.390
Seems you went to a lot of trouble to return it.

00:37:28.510 --> 00:37:29.830
I'm here for only one reason.

00:37:30.890 --> 00:37:32.010
I need a good night's sleep.

00:37:36.970 --> 00:37:39.410
My debt is repaid.

00:38:09.470 --> 00:38:12.130
Your presence here is a violation of the Tau Ceti Accords.

00:38:12.250 --> 00:38:14.210
You lecture us about treaty violations?

00:38:15.170 --> 00:38:16.570
Put down your weapons!

00:38:16.850 --> 00:38:19.170
I know better than to lower my guard around Falcons.

00:38:19.900 --> 00:38:22.330
Look, we're all on the same side here.

00:38:36.970 --> 00:38:37.830
Let's get her to the ship.

00:38:38.460 --> 00:38:39.820
It's no longer your responsibility.

00:38:40.920 --> 00:38:42.620
We'll treat her on the Navarre.

00:38:45.160 --> 00:38:46.360
Still my science officer.

00:38:50.200 --> 00:38:50.500
Close?

00:38:50.780 --> 00:38:51.140
Yes, sir.

00:38:51.330 --> 00:38:51.630
Let's go.

00:39:08.670 --> 00:39:10.590
You should be the one dying, not her.

00:39:27.780 --> 00:39:27.900
She?

00:39:29.400 --> 00:39:29.800
Her injuries?

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:31.040
were quite extensive.

00:39:39.180 --> 00:39:39.640
She lived?

00:39:44.430 --> 00:39:44.970
Wish I could save.

00:39:54.230 --> 00:39:55.170
I know how you must feel.

00:39:56.690 --> 00:39:58.110
She saved my life once, too.

00:40:00.600 --> 00:40:03.660
She can be a real pain in the ass.

00:40:04.780 --> 00:40:06.520
Stubborn, arrogant.

00:40:07.720 --> 00:40:09.480
Sometimes she makes me angry enough

00:40:09.480 --> 00:40:11.810
I want to shove her out an airlock.

00:40:13.010 --> 00:40:15.770
I can understand why the high command's upset,

00:40:17.710 --> 00:40:18.910
but it took a lot of courage

00:40:18.910 --> 00:40:20.610
to step in front of that plasma bullet.

00:40:22.300 --> 00:40:24.340
Do you really want to take her back home in disgrace?

00:40:26.110 --> 00:40:28.150
I think an excuse what she did at the sanctuary.

00:40:28.470 --> 00:40:29.970
I'm not asking anyone to pin a medal on her.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:33.980
All I'm asking is that she be given a second chance.

00:40:41.520 --> 00:40:44.480
If a respected Vulcan captain went before the High Command

00:40:44.480 --> 00:40:47.200
and made a plea on T'Pal's behalf,

00:40:47.970 --> 00:40:50.690
told them how she saved the life of a superior officer,

00:40:53.130 --> 00:40:54.890
wouldn't they think twice about this transfer?

00:40:55.780 --> 00:40:57.260
I can't return without her.

00:40:59.190 --> 00:40:59.970
She suffered extremely...

00:41:00.620 --> 00:41:03.220
I wouldn't advise moving her for quite some time.

00:41:17.660 --> 00:41:19.300
Meeting with the High Command in three days.

00:41:20.840 --> 00:41:26.510
Perhaps there's time. I'll discuss this matter with them.

00:41:28.870 --> 00:41:29.170
Thank you.

00:41:58.320 --> 00:41:58.660
were shot.

00:42:00.090 --> 00:42:00.690
Don't you remember?

00:42:04.460 --> 00:42:05.260
Captain Sobek.

00:42:06.320 --> 00:42:08.050
He's all right, thanks to you.

00:42:12.750 --> 00:42:13.930
I'd like to return to my quarters.

00:42:13.970 --> 00:42:15.390
I'm afraid you're going to have to stay here.

00:42:16.030 --> 00:42:17.760
At least another 24 hours.

00:42:27.890 --> 00:42:29.870
Made quite an impression.

00:42:30.570 --> 00:42:38.720
So I've got a feeling he's going to talk to the high command about that transfer order.

00:42:41.420 --> 00:42:44.100
I'd say the odds are pretty good you're going to be with us for a while longer.

00:42:47.760 --> 00:42:49.420
You should have consulted me first.

00:42:54.260 --> 00:42:56.980
It's probably not too late if you want to catch up to it.

00:43:03.550 --> 00:43:10.160
That won't be possible. Leaving sickbay would violate my doctor's orders.
